{
  "dom_id": "step-e12683",
  "name": "Example: Simplifying a Double Negation",
  "problem": "Simplify the statement $\\neg(\\neg C) \\lor \\neg(\\neg(C \\land D)).$",
  "worked_solution": "Two negations in a row cancel each other out. So: \n\n- we can simplify $\\neg(\\neg C)$ to $C,$ and\n\n- we can also simplify $\\neg(\\neg(C \\land D))$ to $C \\land D.$\n\nTherefore, the given statement can be simplified to \n\n$$\nC \\lor (C \\land D).\n$$",
